            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "csroddin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this with one avocado so I halved the recipe. And since one reviewer said it was salty, I did just 2 tsps of ranch dressing mix, squeezed half a lemon and about 3/4 TB of mayo. It turned out good. Nice avocado spread for sandwiches when you want to change it up a little. I'd make it again."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AttitudeIsEverything"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really liked this spread but i listened to the other reviewers and used 1/2 the ranch dressing. A whole package would have been way too much! I like tangy so i did use 2 tbsp of lemon juice. Was awesome on turkey sandwiches and also as a veggie dip on baby carrots, cucumbers and snap peas. My 12 year old daughter loved it too! Will definitely make this again!",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-10T15:01:33.293Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gloria Sees Through Rain"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This turned out really great. I didn't use the typical Haas avocados because we have green skin avocados which are much larger than regular ones. My avocado was the size of a small pineapple and so I only used one. Since my avocado was so large it wasn't overly salty. I suggest using less dressing mix or adding another avocado. My sandwiches will never be the same again! I think this would be great with other dry mixes as well. Next time I'm going to try taco seasoning or fajita mix or Italian dressing. The possibilities are endless! I'm glad I found this recipe!!",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-06T17:19:59.757Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kahalia"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is my first time ever using an avocado, but I just mixed the avocado, 1 tsp of seasoning salt, and 2 tbsp of lime juice and it was delicious",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-12T17:26:49.193Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Baking Nana"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Based on the other reviews I did not use a whole package of ranch mix - with really nicely ripe avocados you don't need the mayonnaise - light or not it is just added calories. Personally, I prefer lime with avocado - the lemon just didn't taste quite right.",
            "datePublished": "2012-03-13T12:40:29.737Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "1"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "pghsteelergirl79"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really wish I would have read the reviews before I made this. I would have only used 1 or 2 Tbsp of the ranch dressing mix. Made as the recipe is written this is salty and inedible. Normally I read the reviews and alter the recipe accordingly. But, I saw the 4 stars, and just went forward as I was in a hurry. Never again.",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-20T06:07:18.690Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alison Alfredson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Listening to other reviewers I didn't want it to be too salty. I halved the recipe. I used one avocado, Tbsp of fresh lime juice, 1 Tbsp ranch seasoning mix, and a tiny dollop of lite mayo. This was still so tangy I could barely stand it. I added another 1/4 of avocado and that seemed to tone it down just enough. I now have way more than I need for my two grilled chicken sandwiches, but I'm pretty sure it will turn easily into guacamole.",
            "datePublished": "2013-09-22T12:23:55.323Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "c62ru71"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I only used half of the Ranch dressing mix but could have used less as it was still a bit salty. The lemon really made this spread special, nice and tangy and the creamy avocado which were perfectly ripe. yummy... I used it on a turkey, cheese and bacon sandwich (the bacon may have been the salty) and I used it to spread on crackers, it was perfect.",
            "datePublished": "2016-08-09T20:38:34.990Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jeri L"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Way too salty! I think half the amount of seasoning mix would have been plenty. One positive--it does hold its color well.",
            "datePublished": "2009-05-10T19:18:48.657Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
